{"type":"text","timestamp":1771408458991,"sessionID":"ses_38fd5f9a6ffefUclBJV2hWPcpc","part":{"id":"prt_c702bfe9e001cPEqg7rccWDOsT","sessionID":"ses_38fd5f9a6ffefUclBJV2hWPcpc","messageID":"msg_c702b72e7001PY0KwN3R5vsKPy","type":"text","text":"I have implemented request logging using Next.js Middleware. This will intercept requests and log the method and path to the server console.\n\nI created `middleware.ts` in the root directory:\n\n```typescript:middleware.ts\nimport { NextResponse } from 'next/server'\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server'\n\nexport function middleware(request: NextRequest) {\n  // Log the request method and URL to the console\n  console.log(`[${request.method}] ${request.nextUrl.pathname}`)\n  return NextResponse.next()\n}\n\nexport const config = {\n  matcher: [\n    /*\n     * Match all request paths except for the ones starting with:\n     * - _next/static (static files)\n     * - _next/image (image optimization files)\n     * - favicon.ico (favicon file)\n     */\n    '/((?!_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico).*)',\n  ],\n}\n```\n\nThe middleware is configured to run on all routes except for internal Next.js static files (`_next/static`, `_next/image`) and `favicon.ico` to keep the logs clean. If you wish to log literally everything including static assets, you can remove the `matcher` configuration or modify the regex.","time":{"start":1771408458990,"end":1771408458990},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
